## Full-text sources
Only public-domain or openly deposited works are quoted at length. Each carries its own record in
`library/dataset/manifest.json` (`full_text_sources`). Extracted text is presented with normalised
spelling where noted, and always with a locator so a reader can check it against the scan.

## Cite-only sources
Work under copyright is referenced bibliographically and never reproduced: modern practitioner systems
(Stephen Skinner, John Michael Greer, Israel Regardie), the scholarly editions
(M. Charmasson, *Recherches sur une technique divinatoire*, 1980; P. Tannery, *Mémoires scientifiques* II),
and encyclopaedia articles (Encyclopaedia of Islam, "Raml"). If you hold a licence to any of these and
want text included, open an issue with the rights statement and it can be added to the allow-list
deliberately, not accidentally.

## Deliberately excluded
1. **Unofficial uploads of in-copyright books.** Several circulate on document sites. They were inspected
   and not used; nothing here derives from them (see `corpus/raw/ia3/_REMOVED_because_in_copyright.txt`
   in the working tree, and `library/LICENSE_POLICY.md` bucket C).
2. **Living-tradition material.** Ifá odu verses, taboos (ẹ̀wọ) and prescriptions (ẹbọ) belong to a lineage
   and to initiated practitioners; published printings are separately copyrighted. The one Ifá-related
   table present here (`kb/figures.yaml`, the `ifa_odu` column) is a *structural correspondence* taken
   from a modern author who himself warns that sharing sixteen figures does not make the two systems
   behave alike. That warning ships with the data. Do not extend it without the consent and credit of a
   practitioner.
3. **Personal castings.** The screenshots, question text and client context used while building this
   dataset are not redistributed; `data/fixtures/` holds only the abstract figure patterns and explains
   how they were measured.

## About the content
Geomancy is a historical divination method. This repository documents how its practitioners computed and
interpreted, from the sources themselves, including where they contradict each other. It makes no claim
that the method has demonstrated predictive validity. Present it as documentation and as a discipline of
structured reflection, not as a forecast of medical, legal or financial outcomes.
